Synchronization Issue
============================
Tool always execute faster than application
Sometimes application need extra time to load webelement and then it creates
time mapping issue in between application and tool, that is called Synchronization issue in selenium

How to handle it?
-------------------------
Selenium provides two dynamic waits

1.Implicit Wait
-------------------
-Implicit wait is applicable for all webelements
-It is called Global wait
- Apply implicit wait after driver session creates

syntax
----------
driver.manage().timeout().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(10));

If element needs load time is 7sec and implicit wait=10sec then 
as this is dynamic remaining 3sec selenium will not wait it will continue with
next element



2.Explicit Wait
-----------------------
-Explicit wait applicable for single webelement
-Explicit wait we can apply based on conditions

	we use two classes to achieve this wait
	1.WebDriverWait(c)
	2.FluentWait(c)
	
	WebDriverWait(c) extends Fluentwait(c) implements Wait(I)

